WEBVTT

00:03:28.704 --> 00:03:32.163
In addition to monitoring 
the king’s intestinal health,

00:03:32.163 --> 00:03:35.538
the Groom’s... intimate relationship 
with the monarch

00:03:35.538 --> 00:03:38.538
made him a surprisingly
influential figure.

00:03:39.288 --> 00:03:44.288
The next major leap in toilet technology
came in 1596,

00:03:44.288 --> 00:03:48.746
when Sir John Harrington designed 
the first modern flush toilet

00:03:48.746 --> 00:03:49.996
for Queen Elizabeth.

00:03:50.621 --> 00:03:54.996
Its use of levers to release water 
and a valve to drain the bowl

00:03:54.996 --> 00:03:57.538
still inform modern designs.

00:03:57.538 --> 00:04:00.829
But Harrington’s invention 
stank of sewage.